{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892088-other-x20-dark-ages","id":892088,"title":"Other X20 Dark Ages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-16T16:05:36-07:00","id":892088,"title":"Other X20 Dark Ages","content":"So V20 Dark Ages pulled down nearly $300k during its Kickstarter run and is a Platinum seller on DriveThruRPG. Do you think the success it enjoyed means there's any chance of the other Dark Ages lines getting revived? DA: Fae is well-loved even by fans who loathe Changeling: the Dreaming, and I'm sure Werewolf and Mage fans wouldn't complain about new content; Inquisitor was a fun experiment that felt really different from Hunter: the Reckoning, while Wraith was cut short before ever getting to enjoy a Dark Ages book?<br /> <br /> Anyone else here hoping for this? I've always preferred the Dark Ages take on Vampire over the modern day, but it seems lile a shame to let them have all the fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:25:05-07:00","id":892101,"title":"","content":"I would love to see Malcolm and/or David Hill Jr. and the rest of the DAV20 team take on Dark Ages Mage. It had a unique take on expressing the themes of Mage through its Foundation and Pillar system and I'd love to see that revamped and expanded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:09:52-07:00","id":892128,"title":"","content":"If DAV20 was meant to be more like DAV Revised, I'd be more optimistic about it. Since it was more along the lines of VDA I'm not so sure about any push to do DA lines for the rest of the games.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure that the Dark Ages thing is the best way to go. Shattered Dreams is sort of the W20 &quot;past era&quot; book already. I could see it be more of the trend for the X20s to pick a time period that suits the game line than revive the DA Revised &quot;every game line&quot; thing. DA Mage has a lot of fans (and not fans), but the Sorcerer's Crusade era is probably more compelling as a setting even if the SC rules are closer to base-line Mage. Changeling has a few interesting time-periods to explore, as does Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T22:48:35-07:00","id":892305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892088-other-x20-dark-ages?p=892128#post892128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If DAV20 was meant to be more like DAV Revised, I'd be more optimistic about it. Since it was more along the lines of VDA I'm not so sure about any push to do DA lines for the rest of the games.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure that the Dark Ages thing is the best way to go. Shattered Dreams is sort of the W20 &quot;past era&quot; book already. I could see it be more of the trend for the X20s to pick a time period that suits the game line than revive the DA Revised &quot;every game line&quot; thing. DA Mage has a lot of fans (and not fans), but the Sorcerer's Crusade era is probably more compelling as a setting even if the SC rules are closer to base-line Mage. Changeling has a few interesting time-periods to explore, as does Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, DA: Mage, Fae, and Inquisitor are mechanically distinct enough from their modern heirs as to basically be their own games that happen to share a background. I've always said that Vampire's weird Biblical mythology grounds it far better in the Dark Ages than today, and that the High/Low Clan divide feels much more organic (and gives players more options!) than the big Sects. I like Dark Ages as basically a separate universe from the World of Darkness, and would love to see it prosper on its own! Wraith has one of its Great Maelstroms during the Black Plague, which is conceivably during the Dark Ages time period, and the whole affair with the Fishers and other Heretics being a major faction alongside the Hierarchy is worthy of exploration.<br /> <br /> None of this takes away from other time periods, though; I'm still dying to see Victorian Mage. I just would really like some more love for the Dark Ages games, partly because they feel so much more coherent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T05:32:05-07:00","id":892435,"title":"","content":"And don't forget that a DA Wraith game would be set <i>before</i> the Breaking of the Guilds, meaning they would be there in the open and heavily involved in politics.<br /> <br /> Yet more reasons why I want DAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T12:15:37-07:00","id":892689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892088-other-x20-dark-ages?p=892435#post892435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't forget that a DA Wraith game would be set <i>before</i> the Breaking of the Guilds, meaning they would be there in the open and heavily involved in politics.<br /> <br /> Yet more reasons why I want DAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between that and the Book of Oblivion, Wraith books seem to have the best abbreviations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:29:22-07:00","id":892867,"title":"","content":"Well technically Dark Ages Werewolf is DAW while Dark Ages Wraith would be DAWr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:57:45-07:00","id":892873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/892088-other-x20-dark-ages?p=892867#post892867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well technically Dark Ages Werewolf is DAW while Dark Ages Wraith would be DAWr.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's hilariously dissonant! (^VVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:28:35-07:00","id":892950,"title":"","content":"In the Old Forum. The MachineIV mentioned that he would also like to produce.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages Wraith 20<br /> Dark Ages Mage 20<br /> Dark Ages Fae 20<br /> Dark Ages Werewolf 20.<br /> <br /> There will also be a book about Hunted Hunters and Infernalismo (who I believe had demons, too).<br /> <br /> ________________________________<br /> <br /> And I believe we should have a forum on Line Dark Ages, here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","user":"Ben Linus","date":". 05-19-2016, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T04:53:48-07:00","id":898813,"title":"","content":"Once again i express my hope that, in the upcoming 4th edition, nWW (new White Wolf) will have a unified world with one corebook to rule them all (similar to CofD). One could then create one supplement that ports Vampire, Mage, Werewolf etc. to the Dark Ages, with updated rules and descriptions of the various supernatural societies the existed back then.<br /> <br /> The only problems i see with this way is that you need three books to run a DA Vampire game (Corebook, Vampire and Dark Ages) and that one book might not be enough to explain the various differences between the modern day games and the Dark Ages ones (for example, diffrences between DA Foundation/Pillars and MD Arete/Spheres for Mage).<br /> <br /> One way to solve this could be to, for example, have one corebook and each splat gets one DA and one MD &quot;core&quot; supplement. That way you only need two books and you get a whole lot more room to explain the diffrences between the DA setting and the MD setting for each supplement. This does mean that there will be more DA books (at least one for each splat) but that also means more money for nWW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}